# Copy to .env.local for local development. On Vercel, set the same names under Project > Settings > Environment Variables.
# Nothing here has a default. Without these, learners still see everything except videos, and the editor desk stays switched off.

# --- Editor desk (/studio) -------------------------------------------------
# The password editors type in. At least 12 characters. Use a long random one.
EDITOR_PASSWORD=
# Signs the editor's session cookie. At least 32 random characters, for example the output of:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
EDITOR_SESSION_SECRET=

# --- Teacher accounts and the Drawer -----------------------------------------
# Signs the teacher session cookie. Optional: when it is not set, EDITOR_SESSION_SECRET is used (signed for a
# different purpose). With neither, teacher sign-in is switched off. Teacher data uses the same Redis store below.
TEACHER_SESSION_SECRET=

# --- Where video entries are saved ------------------------------------------
# Needed on Vercel (its file system is read-only). Create a Redis store (for example Upstash Redis from the
# Vercel Marketplace; it has a free tier, but it is a separate account) and connect it to this project.
# Either pair of names works:
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
# KV_REST_API_URL=
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
# Locally, with none of these set, entries are saved to .data/videos.json instead.
